# `journal.jsonl` is always versioned (docs/adr/0008-the-journal-is-versioned-
# and-the-vault-is-local.md) and strictly append-only, so two clones append at
# the same end of the same file and any merge of them conflicts. A conflicted
# journal is an unparseable journal, and an unparseable journal is refused
# outright: `init` and `journal` both gate on it until someone repairs the
# file by hand. (`status` does not gate on it -- it never reads either
# journal, so a conflicted one leaves it reporting a clean project.) Git's
# built-in union driver keeps both sides' appended lines instead of writing
# conflict markers, and needs no per-clone configuration.
#
# Deliberately not anchored to the repository root: an adopter root is not
# always a repository root, and matching one journal too many costs nothing
# beside missing the one that matters.
#
# This covers this repository's own journal only. Attributes do not travel
# between repositories: an adopter needs the same line in its own
# `.gitattributes`, and `init` does not write it there today.
journal.jsonl merge=union
